bye and keep da warez rollin'


                    08/01/94 [---> WiLD THiNG - Mannassas - DiXiE BBS <---]
@endnode

@node overview
                          --- F E A T U R E S ---

· scans for new topics at login and lists them
· everyone can add/delete topics and items to vote on (access level
  depending, differs on every topic if a user can add items or not)
· creates complete result list for free download at wish
· users votes will be stored, so he can look where he voted on and change
  his vote - everyone can vote only once
· results are shown sorted with percentage and graph bars
· info who and when somebody created a topic and optional long description
· optional logs to callerslog


              *** THIS DOOR DOESN'T CONTAIN ANY BACKDOORS ***

The  only  'hidden'  function  is  the  command 'q' which will exit without
saving(for access higher than 250)

@endnode

@node installation
                      --- I N S T A L L A T I O N --

Because  this  is just a beta release you'll have to create the first topic
by  hand  or  change  the  one  in  the arc.  There has to be a file called
tems.WV in the Doors:WildTools/Wildvote/ directory which contains:

                     first line  - number of topics
                     second line - name of the topics
                     third line  - access level needed to add item

in the Doors:WildTools/Wildvote/tems/ directory are the files with the
votes and the names of each topic their names are the numbers of the
topic. e.g: file 1(KeWLeST BBS):
=== cut here ===
DiXiE   <------- name of the item
4       <------- number of votes
Mamba
4
Crazy World
4
=== cut here ===
If  you  want  WiLDVote  to  be started automatically at every logon and to
check  if  a  user hasn't voted on a topic yet you'll have to use two names
for  it,  for  the auto-start it MUST be 'WVC' for the other anything else.
Now put the ~CC_WVC command to your bull.txt.
The  problem  is  that  WiLDVote shouldn't be used at more than one node at
once  but  as  WiLDVote has two different names there might be some problem
with the stats files.
WV is an AIM type door, MULTINODE=NO

Have a look at the WiLDVote.cfg file, here the access levels for the
different actions are defined.

@endnode

